## 3. Review Finding 45 — independent convergence on the same production-prose defect

Finding 45 and my own read land on the same sentence,
`analyzer_helpers.go:184-192`: *"A binder omits a variant only when the binder itself is
enabled-but-not-binding … which is precisely the condition under which its own sizing is
untrustworthy."*

- **My proof (binder side):** TA is the binder in `[sat-not-live] + [TA]`, fully live and
  informative, and still omits any zero-replica variant lacking persisted supply
  (`throughput/analyzer.go:385-414`). A healthy binder omitting variants is normal operation.
- **Its proof (predicate side):** `ResultIsInformative` is an **any-variant** predicate
  (`analyzer_helpers.go:53+`), so aggregate-informative ≠ per-variant-priced.

Same conclusion, two directions; its version generalizes further. The `N8` conclusion (do not borrow
saturation's sizing) may well survive — the carrier/binder split and the metric-scale argument at
`:189-192` are independent and do stand — but **this sentence is not the reason**, and it is shipping
in production prose. Its suggested repair (rest the refusal on `:189-192`) is the right one.

